The principal-geometry page also records the choice convention: the smooth tangent-bundle and vector-field construction used by the horizontal-connection item inherits \(\mathrm{AC}_\omega\); the definition of a gauge automorphism and its action on associated fibers do not select from a family. The local gauge branch should state exactly which result introduces that assumption and avoid copying it to choice-free calculations.

The root contains useful mathematical context that is not in the current physics import snapshot. In particular, **library/homological-algebra/bv-brst-and-homological-physics-interfaces.md** lists **def-bv-algebra-and-degree-plus-one-bracket**, **thm-bv-derived-bracket-is-odd-poisson**, **def-classical-and-formal-quantum-master-equations**, **thm-classical-master-equation-defines-square-zero-differential**, **def-classical-lie-action-brst-complex**, and **thm-classical-lie-action-brst-differential-squares-zero**. The six actual item files currently have status: published, but none of their IDs occurs in physics/research/math-imports.json; the page prose still says the items remain drafts. Reconcile this source/page/import mismatch before treating them as active physics dependencies. Their exact mathematics is a degree-\(+1\) BV convention and a classical Chevalley–Eilenberg complex from a Lie algebra action by derivations. The page expressly excludes the full Koszul–Tate/BFV construction, reducible and open algebras, and quantum BRST cohomology. The local non-Abelian finite-jet complex still needs its own definition and theorem.

The completed root math run **inverse-problems-knot-theory-all-109-2026-10-19** was checked from the live .autopilot/ status and Git history on 2026-10-23; the run status is COMPLETE. **def-asd-moduli-fredholm-index-and-lattice-setup** and **thm-asd-deformation-complex-index-formula** are root-published but absent from the current physics import snapshot. **thm-charge-one-self-dual-su-two-connections-on-the-round-four-sphere-are-bpst** is a draft and not imported. **lem-euclidean-asd-energy-concentration-is-finite** is an untracked item file, and the weak Coulomb ASD regularity helpers remain drafts outside the physics snapshot. These files are candidate mathematics context only. They do not certify a four-dimensional Yang–Mills quantum theory, a local proof in this physics category, or the completeness of instanton compactness/regularity arguments.

## Existing QFT and gauge carriers, by current physics files

