| **physics/library/quantum-field-theory/qft-g02.md**: **post-qft-formal-qed-coefficients**, **post-qft-compact-lattice-gauge-model**, **pthm-qft-lattice-gauge-existence**, **pthm-qft-lattice-gauge-ward**; supporting **def-qft-compact-lattice-gauge-data** | The finite lattice model is a finite oriented graph with compact \(U(1)\) rotors on links, finite CAR matter, integer electric operators, an explicit Hamiltonian domain and Gauss operators. Its published physical theorems establish a nonzero finite-regulator Gauss sector, unitary dynamics and selected finite-regulator Ward/Gauss identities under their stated assumptions. | This is not non-Abelian \(G\)-valued link data, not an infinite lattice theorem, not a continuum limit, not interacting continuum QED, not a proof of confinement, and not a Yang–Mills existence or mass-gap supplier. The formal QED coefficients are not a convergent series or an all-loop gauge-independence theorem. |
