items/thm-every-orbit-is-an-injectively-immersed-homogeneous-space.md:62:3.1 By [F2], the quotient map $q:G\to G/G_x$ is a submersion and has smooth local sections. Since $\Phi_x=\overline\Phi_x\circ q$, on the domain of such a section $s$ one has $\overline\Phi_x=\Phi_x\circ s$, proving smoothness. If $v\in T_{eG_x}(G/G_x)$ and $d\overline\Phi_x(v)=0$, choose $X\in\mathfrak g$ with $dq_eX=v$. Then $d\Phi_x(X)=0$, so [F3] gives $X\in T_eG_x=\ker dq_e$ and hence $v=0$. Equivariance from step 2.1 transports this injectivity to every coset. Thus the factor is an injective immersion. [F2, F3, step 1.1, step 2.1]

