## Example

Let $M=\mathbb R^2$ with coordinates $(x,y)$, let $G=SU(2)$, and let $P=M\times G$ have the right action $(z,g)h=(z,gh)$. Use the defining representation on $V=\mathbb C^2$ with its standard positive-definite Hermitian form $h(v,w)=v^*w$, and let $E=P\times_G\mathbb C^2$. Set

$$
T_3=-\frac{i}{2}\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\0&-1\end{pmatrix},\qquad
u(x,y)=\begin{pmatrix}e^{-ix/2}&0\\0&e^{ix/2}\end{pmatrix},\qquad
A=u^{-1}du=T_3\,dx.
$$

Equip $P$ with the principal form


