+# Batch 2 — `qftx-gauge-geometry`
+
+## Scope and plan comparison
+
+The current canonical plan row in `research/plan-spec.json` matches the assigned A page identity, title, `mathematics` library, companion, and five required imported pages. The current design section in `research/plan-advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry-track.md` matches its global-bundle, principal-form, curvature, gauge-covariance, Bianchi, and associated-derivative scope and lists the four planned item IDs. `plan-spec.json` has an A row with the B companion named; the B row is present in the current batch manifest. No current claim or prerequisite conflict is found.
+
+The noncanonical `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/plan-fragment.json` assigns this pair order 2, while the current canonical plan and dispatch assign order 958. The canonical plan controls; authored A/B page order is 958. The broader gauge-theory material in `research-gauge.md` is a research programme; this assigned pair supplies the mathematical geometry interface only.
+
+The exact imported principal-connection definition supplies a horizontal complement and vertical-valued curvature, not a \(\mathfrak g\)-valued form or Cartan formula. Its declared axiom base carries exactly \(\mathrm{AC}_\omega\). The four proposed contracts also omit the direct Lie-group tangent-algebra theorem needed to identify \(\mathfrak g=T_eG\), and they do not define the graded bracket of Lie-algebra-valued forms. Both are supplied explicitly in the authoring dependency map below; no full Axiom of Choice is introduced.
+
