'def-qftx-associated-covariant-derivative':r'''1.1 On a principal chart, each "'$p'"\\in\\pi"'^{-1}(U_i)$ has a unique expression $p=s_i(x)h$. The associated-bundle chart therefore assigns $[s_i(x)h,v]$ the vector coordinate $'"\\rho(h)v"'$. In particular $[s_i(x),'"\\psi_i(x)]"'$ determines a unique smooth component $'"\\psi_i"'$. If $s_j=s_i g_{ij}$, then $[s_j,'"\\psi_j]=[s_i,\\rho(g_{ij})\\psi_j]"'$; equality with $[s_i,'"\\psi_i]"'$ gives $'"\\psi_j=\\rho(g_{ij}"'^{-1})'"\\psi_i"'$. [F1, F2, F3, given]

