+# Batch 2 — `qftx-gauge-geometry`
+
+## Scope and plan comparison
+
+The current canonical plan row in `research/plan-spec.json` matches the assigned A page identity, title, `mathematics` library, companion, and five required imported pages. The current design section in `research/plan-advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry-track.md` matches its global-bundle, principal-form, curvature, gauge-covariance, Bianchi, and associated-derivative scope and lists the four planned item IDs. `plan-spec.json` has an A row with the B companion named; the B row is present in the current batch manifest. No current claim or prerequisite conflict is found.
+
+The noncanonical `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/plan-fragment.json` assigns this pair order 2, while the current canonical plan and dispatch assign order 958. The canonical plan controls; authored A/B page order is 958. The broader gauge-theory material in `research-gauge.md` is a research programme; this assigned pair supplies the mathematical geometry interface only.
+
+The exact imported principal-connection definition supplies a horizontal complement and vertical-valued curvature, not a \(\mathfrak g\)-valued form or Cartan formula. Its declared axiom base carries exactly \(\mathrm{AC}_\omega\). The four proposed contracts also omit the direct Lie-group tangent-algebra theorem needed to identify \(\mathfrak g=T_eG\), and they do not define the graded bracket of Lie-algebra-valued forms. Both are supplied explicitly in the authoring dependency map below; no full Axiom of Choice is introduced.
+
+## Item inventory and in-run levels
+
+| Item | Level | Direct in-run suppliers | Current claim/convention |
+|---|---:|---|---|
+| `def-qftx-nonabelian-gauge-data` | 0 | — | Selected compact noncommutative Lie group with its actual global form, smooth right bundle, specified unitary representations and their associated bundles, and declared admitted bundle sectors; \(\mathfrak g=\operatorname{Lie}(G)\) uses the imported left-invariant bracket convention and \(\mathrm{AC}_\omega\). Direct external inputs: `def-countable-choice`, `def-lie-group`, `thm-the-tangent-space-at-the-identity-is-a-lie-algebra`, `def-principal-g-bundle-and-associated-fiber-bundle`, `def-smooth-principal-g-bundle`, `def-finite-dimensional-representation-of-a-group-over-a-field`, `def-associated-bundle-to-a-principal-bundle-and-representation`, `thm-associated-vector-bundle-is-well-defined`. |
+| `def-qftx-principal-connection-form` | 0 | — | Constructs \(\omega_p=\zeta_p^{-1}v_p\) from the given horizontal splitting; fixes the right-action fundamental-vector and \(\operatorname{Ad}_{g^{-1}}\) conventions, proves the converse correspondence, and defines \(\kappa_H=\omega\circ K_H\). Direct external inputs include `def-principal-connection-and-vertical-curvature`, `thm-the-tangent-space-at-the-identity-is-a-lie-algebra`, `def-exponential-map-of-a-lie-group`, `thm-one-parameter-subgroups-are-integral-curves-of-left-invariant-fields`, and the adjoint/differential suppliers; the input chain retains \(\mathrm{AC}_\omega\). |
+| `def-qftx-lie-algebra-valued-form-bracket` | 0 | — | Newly authored local definition/proof of the shuffle bracket, graded skew-symmetry, graded Jacobi, and componentwise exterior-derivative rule; this missing operation is needed before the curvature lemma. It is the one `inventory_expansion_required` item added on the assigned A page. |
+| `lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi` | 1 | `def-qftx-principal-connection-form`, `def-qftx-lie-algebra-valued-form-bracket` | Proves \(\Omega_\omega=d\omega+\tfrac12[\omega\wedge\omega]=\omega\circ K_H\), horizontality, \(\operatorname{Ad}\)-equivariance, local section/gauge transition formulas, and \(D_A F_A=0\) in the stated right-action/left-Maurer convention. |
+| `def-qftx-associated-covariant-derivative` | 1 | `def-qftx-principal-connection-form` | For a specified smooth finite-dimensional complex representation, defines \(\rho_*=d\rho_e\) and the associated operator \(d\psi_i+\rho_*(A_i)\psi_i\); proves patching under \(s_j=s_i g_{ij}\), with \(\psi_j=\rho(g_{ij}^{-1})\psi_i\) and \(A_j=\operatorname{Ad}_{g_{ij}^{-1}}A_i+g_{ij}^{-1}dg_{ij}\), and proves the Leibniz rule. It does not rely on a missing curvature carrier. |
+| `ex-qftx-su2-flat-pure-gauge-connection` | 2 | `lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi` (and A-page definitions) | On \(\mathbb R^2\times SU(2)\), takes \(u=\operatorname{diag}(e^{-ix/2},e^{ix/2})\), \(A=u^{-1}du=T_3dx\); verifies \(SU(2)\) is compact/noncommutative, realizes the form as a smooth right-principal connection, and proves \(A\ne0\), \(F=0\). |
+| `ex-qftx-su2-noncommuting-curvature` | 2 | `lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi`, `def-qftx-associated-covariant-derivative` | Independently verifies \(SU(2)\) compact/noncommutative, uses \(A=T_1dx+T_2dy\), \(T_a=-i\sigma_a/2\), checks \([T_1,T_2]=T_3\), derives \(F=T_3dx\wedge dy\), and directly computes \([\nabla_x,\nabla_y]=T_3\) on every smooth defining-representation section. No dependency on the other B example. |
+
+The remaining assigned items are to be added supplier-first. The batch scheduling record gives batch 2 level 0 with no in-run page prerequisites; all five named page prerequisites are imported mathematical context. The only cross-batch consumer is downstream and belongs to its owning batch; this file will contain only edges whose consumer is owned by batch 2.
+
+## Source reading and harvested-result ledger
+
+The full relevant reasoning in both independent treatments was inspected directly. No source retrieval failed, so no recovery retry or `source_resolution` disposition is needed. The local proofs below do not cite a source as a substitute for an argument.
+
+1. **Matthijs Vákár, “Principal Bundles and Gauge Theories,” arXiv:2110.06334** — [full HTML](https://arxiv.org/html/2110.06334). Read §§1.1.3, 1.1.5, 1.3.1, 1.3.3, 1.4.1, and 2.1 in full. §1.1.3/1.1.5 supports the right-principal/associated quotient conventions (`def-qftx-nonabelian-gauge-data`); §1.3.1 proves the orbit differential isomorphism, connection-form reproduction/equivariance, Cartan formula and Bianchi identity (`def-qftx-principal-connection-form`, `def-qftx-lie-algebra-valued-form-bracket`, `lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi`); §§1.3.3/1.4.1 support induced associated connections and local covariant-derivative form (`def-qftx-associated-covariant-derivative`); §2.1 distinguishes bundle automorphisms from local functions into the group. Disposition: all four assigned claims are independently proved locally; the source is supporting context, not a logical proof supplier.
+
+2. **Karl-Hermann Neeb, “Differential Topology of Fiber Bundles,” full lecture notes (2024)** — [full PDF](https://www.math.fau.de/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/bundle-lect.pdf). Read Chapter 1 §§1.4, 1.6; Chapter 5 §5.4; and Chapter 6 §6.1 in full. These sections support smooth principal/associated bundles, connection 1-form axioms and recovery of the horizontal distribution, the right-action transition law, curvature horizontality/equivariance, and the local Cartan expression (`def-qftx-nonabelian-gauge-data`, `def-qftx-principal-connection-form`, `def-qftx-lie-algebra-valued-form-bracket`, `lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi`, `def-qftx-associated-covariant-derivative`). Disposition: local arguments and exact conventions are reproduced and checked in the item proofs; no quantum, physical, or path-integral claim is taken from the source.
